Attribute What it holds <code>status_code</code> The HTTP status, e.g. <code>422</code>. <code>detail</code> The server's explanation, from its error body. Falls back to the body text, truncated. <code>errors</code> Per-item problems from the error body, if any (for example one per failing tag-list handle). <code>code</code> The server's machine-readable error code, if any. <code>hint</code> What to do about it, when the library knows (auth and rate-limit errors). <code>method</code>, <code>url</code> The request, with any secret key in the URL masked. <code>response</code> The full <code>httpx2.Response</code>. <p>The message reads like <code>422 Unprocessable Entity from POST /v2/items/discontinue: &lt;detail&gt;</code>, with the hint on the next line when there is one.</p> <pre><code>import t3api_utils as t3

try:
    client.post("/v2/items/discontinue", license="LIC-00001", json={"id": 12345}, submit=True)
except t3.ValidationError as exc:
    print("Rejected:", exc.detail)
    for problem in exc.errors:
        print("  ", problem)
except t3.AuthError as exc:
    print(exc.hint)
    raise
</code></pre>
